SUMMARY:reTURN the Favor Public Walk: Norbury’s Landing/Sunray Beach
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a reTURN the Favor walk organized by New Jersey Audubon to help rescue stranded horseshoe crabs and learn more about them along the way. This event is great for all ages. Be sure to wear shoes that can get wet\, and be prepared for the conditions\, including bug spray and sun protection. \nPREREGISTRATION REQUIRED – ticket sales end 24hrs before the start of the event \n\n\nCOST: FREE \n\n\nInterested in becoming a member? Please click on the following link to learn more or join: Become a Member today! \nMEETING LOCATION: Meet at Norbury’s Landing at the end of Millman Boulevard in Del Haven\, NJ. \n\n\nIMPORTANT INFORMATION:  \nWe bird (and crab) in all weather. Be sure to check the forecast in advance and dress in layers appropriate for prevailing weather conditions. The weather in Cape May can differ considerably from nearby inland areas and may be warmer\, colder\, or windier so it’s best to be over prepared. We may have to bird in the rain\, so please bring your rain gear. \n\n\nTRANSPORTATION: We may walk up to 1.5 miles\, over generally level\, sometimes muddy or sandy terrain. Some trips involve walks over jetties. \nIf you’d like to learn more about reTURN the Favor\, click here: reTURN the Favor – Horseshoe Crab Rescue Program (returnthefavornj.org) \nCANCELLATION: NJ Audubon’s CMBO programs are virtually never cancelled. If we cancel\, due to lack of participation\, severe weather\, or unforeseen circumstances\, all participants will be notified as soon as possible and are eligible for a full refund. Participants may cancel without penalty if greater than 48 hours in advance. Sorry\, no refund for cancellations less than 48 hours in advance unless due to health emergencies; however\, registrations can be transferred to another program in the future. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/return-the-favor-public-walk-norburys-landing-3/
LOCATION:Norbury’s Landing\, 2-98 N Delaware Ave\, Villas\, NJ\, 08251\, United States
CATEGORIES:Cape May Bird Observatory,Cape May Bird Observatory's Northwood Center,Family Program,Nature Walk
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Return-the-Favor-2024-EventBrite.png
GEO:39.0502428;-74.9271662
